<!--

Tier 1: Terrathyst Crucible:
-Creates only basic and genesite items.
-Creates normal weapons and items.
-High crafting speed
-Low stone extraction output

Tier 1: Terrathyst Charger:
-Charges tier 1 and 2 gear at a low rate
-Evolves lithic weapons
-1 item capacity

Tier 2: Chronite Forge:
-Creates Tier 2 gear
-Normal crafting speed
-Better stone extraction output

-->

<!--Guide for T1 recycling:
    -T1 only returns steel.
    -Return on materials is 1/4th of the ingredients, rounded to nearest whole.
    -Normal components always add 1 shocksap
    -Advanced components add 3 shocksap
    -Add +3 steel for every components used
    -Cannot convert structures
    -Armor produces Endosap instead of shocksap
    -Supports up to Microelectronics, and only craftable items-->

<Defs>
  <ThingDef ParentName="BenchBase">
    <defName>ET_TerrathystCrucible</defName> <!--Tier 1-->
    <label>terrathyst crucible</label>
    <description>A small crystal structure with its own shocksap pool. This structure allows a tribe to shape a limited amount of lithic items and weapons.
The crucible's own shocksap reserve is self-sustaining, and small enough to replenish without running out. This allows it to be effectively unlimited; however, the tiny volume requires the user to supply additional shocksap during most processes. 
While this crucible is a good starting point and can always prove useful, there is a lithic structure out there that does every crafting aspect of the terrathyst crucible better.</description>
